{"name":"Grey Silt","hex":"#b0a99a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"silt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mud or fine earth deposited from running or standing water.","Any material with similar physical characteristics, regardless of its origins or transport."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clog or fill with silt.","To become clogged with silt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silt","blocks":[{"text":"Silt is granular material of a size between sand and clay and composed mostly of broken grains of quartz. Silt may occur as a soil or as sediment mixed in suspension with water. Silt usually has a floury feel when dry, and lacks plasticity when wet. Silt can also be felt by the tongue as granular when placed on the front teeth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Windrow_of_windblown_glacial_silt%2C_NWT.jpg/330px-Windrow_of_windblown_glacial_silt%2C_NWT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silt","wikidata":"Q270699"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org